# Code quality

- TypeScript strict mode; avoid `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow safely.
- Prefer small named functions and explicit types.
- Keep UI components focused on presentation and interaction.
- TanStack Query owns remote/API data; Zustand owns cart and small client-only UI state.
- Do not duplicate server state in Zustand.
- Use server pagination; never load the entire catalog to filter in the browser.
- Include loading, empty, error and success states.
- Use semantic accessible HTML and keyboard-operable controls.
- Add tests for business rules, validation, authorization and critical API behavior.
- Do not claim tests/build/lint passed unless the command was executed.
- After a phase run lint, typecheck and relevant tests; report exact results.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies, premature abstractions and unrelated refactors.
